; FOR-JOSEPH — the running thoughts/decisions-to-run-by-you queue.
; Started 2026-07-28 at Joseph's request. Expectation set by him: no
; satisfying YES/NO at this stage — he uses these to surface issues with
; the decisions either way (more brainstorm fuel, DISCUSSION-THOUGHTS
; style). Items get :status open until his reaction lands; reactions
; route to spikes/schema-review/DISCUSSION-THOUGHTS.udon or wherever
; they belong. Sibling registers: OPEN.md (formal steward calls),
; spikes/schema-review/DISCUSSION-THOUGHTS.udon (his brainstorms).

|item[staging-question] :date 2026-07-28 :status open :class direction
  The meta-call under the fixture question: do the schema / paths /
  dialects / types / embeds territories force any IMMEDIATE change to
  0.9.1, or do they all stage for future versions? Joseph's stated
  posture: the spec should be written better than the old one — ready
  to CHANGE, not ready to reimplement yet; avoid premature
  calcification. Either way has issues worth his eye: staging
  everything keeps 0.9.1 clean but lets the four maps drift from the
  text they cite; immediate changes calcify exactly the territory the
  spikes haven't run. A middle route: 0.9.1 stays frozen, and each
  territory map carries a would-change register (what 0.9.1 sentences
  it would touch, if ratified) so the future merge is pre-staged
  without any text moving.

|item[fixture-posture] :date 2026-07-28 :status open :class deferred-lean
  Given staging-question, the full 0.9.1 fixture suite is deferred —
  the interesting fixtures wait on that call, and the boring ones would
  mostly mirror the 0.9 groups. What might still be worth having now:
  a THIN descriptive group pinning only the settled core (TUTORIAL
  scope), framed per S2, as reading-companion rather than gate — the
  concretely-sitting-next-to-it affordance Joseph named, without
  calcifying anything open.

|item[steward-calls] :date 2026-07-28 :status open :class queue
  Eleven formal calls queued in OPEN.md. Highest leverage per minute:
  REF-SLASH and REF-BRACKET (gate the include-primitive direction),
  ROOT-BASE (gates whole-document schema; one instance of the
  element-centric/root-silent defect class worth a systematic sweep),
  LINEAGE (who owns identity-over-time). Also pending: SEMI-BASE, S4,
  FIX-FRAME, N-jargon, IND/IND-2, GOV-REGIME, DEBT-DISCHARGE.
  Offer: assemble the top four into one adjudication packet with
  three-way facts each, for a single sitting.

|item[pass-1-deletion] :date 2026-07-28 :status open :class housekeeping
  spikes/schema-ideation/pass-1-explication.md — the schema agent's O2
