  you asked. Delete after your comparison, or keep as the record of the
  register lesson?

|item[priorities-bridge] :date 2026-07-28 :status open :class proposal
  Your "I don't know what that would look like": concretely, one
  document — each demand cluster from the tooling corpus (guarded edit,
  addressing, context economy, persistence, ...) crossed against the
  four new supply maps, yielding per-demand: what supply now exists,
  what spike would close the gap, what it waits on, and a rank by
  (demand strength x supply readiness). Where the old
  priorities-and-spike-agenda predates tonight, this supersedes it.
  Precondition I hold myself to: reading the seven deep reports first
  (my demand-side picture is currently secondhand). Deliverable shape:
  udon-needs/02-tooling-needs/ sibling or v2/spikes/ — your lean
  welcome.

|item[reader-declaration-experiment] :date 2026-07-28 :status open :class proposal
  The concrete answer to "what are you proposing" on O5's reader-half
  (the architecture's least-supported load-bearing assumption: that
  consumers will DECLARE what they read). Hand-rolled, a day: take the
  three or four real consumers on this machine (vivarium bin/check,
  asf extract-findings, the OUTLINE generator, relata emit), write
  each one's read-declaration by hand (which elements/attributes/paths
  it consumes), then check three things — is declaring cheap and
  natural; would drift-detection against these declarations have
  caught real past incidents (the renamed slug); do they feel
  maintainable or like a fifth language. Evidence either way feeds O5
  before anything is built on it.

|item[tst-grounding-agent] :date 2026-07-28 :status launched :class commission
  Per your #3: exploration agent launched (opus) — starting from the
  asf dossier in udon-needs syntheses, then the TST segments whole plus
  adjacent theory and the udon-needs segments that elaborate them.
  Charter: what TST already supplies for the payment-time/four-whens,
  strata-clocks, co-location/coupling, and expand-contract questions —
  and what mathematics is genuinely missing. Report expected at
  spikes/tst-grounding/.

|item[commit-cadence] :date 2026-07-28 :status adopted :class norm
  Committing as we go, coherent commits per body of work. Five landed
  for this session (b1d060c..e2b3fcf); this file and successors ride
  the next one.
